{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/540366-beasts-primordial-s-changeling-spoiler","id":540366,"title":"Beasts: Primordial's Changeling Spoiler","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-04T19:27:44-07:00","id":540366,"title":"Beasts: Primordial's Changeling Spoiler","content":"Spoiler Alert<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Beast's Draft has a spoiler for Changeling, it appears that Toyko's Courts are ruled by Moon Princesses, that they're court system is based on a story called the Bamboo Cutter's Tale, that they have 12 ambassadors to other Supernatural Races, that the Freehold extends over the greater Toyko area. It seems this Freehold might be big by the sounds of it, makes sense as its Toyko.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T20:54:52-07:00","id":540490,"title":"","content":"Best Official Freehold Ever!<br /> <br /> No disrespect for Miami, but that write up didn't exactly speak to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T13:08:07-07:00","id":541619,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://www.sacred-texts.com/shi/jft2/jft208.htm\" target=\"_blank\">Here's</a> a link to the story. It might help fuel speculation on how they deal with the Huntsmen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Currently Playing:</b> <i>A large, mixed splat game of <b>CofD</b>.</i> <b>As:</b> Seraph du Salomon, Voice on the concordance. Unsubtle man reluctantly participating in the business of Magi. Awakening 2E homebrew <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1338514-house-du-salomon-a-proximus-dynasty?_=1569864567692\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...=1569864567692</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2598-gryphon-s-feather","name":"Gryphon's Feather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2598_3.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"215"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T23:41:47-07:00","id":544857,"title":"","content":"12?! What species are large enough, that didn't get their own book, to require that many?! There are ten including Beast, so if we take out Changeling and hunter we have eight for the main and four that we may not know about. Hmmmmmm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1110,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1110-unjustcustos","user":"UnjustCustos","date":". 06-08-2015, 02:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1110-unjustcustos","name":"UnjustCustos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T03:15:00-07:00","id":544955,"title":"","content":"Ghosts &amp; Spirits do not have their own lines, the Kitsune from Skinchangers also reside in Japan. The Cursed of Hachiko in Hurt Locker also come from Tokyo.<br /> <br /> So that is at least 3 options.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T03:54:27-07:00","id":544972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>UnjustCustos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/540366-beasts-primordial-s-changeling-spoiler?p=544857#post544857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">12?! What species are large enough, that didn't get their own book, to require that many?! There are ten including Beast, so if we take out Changeling and hunter we have eight for the main and four that we may not know about. Hmmmmmm.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe in Japan Humans Would count as a seperate Species, I think it would be something like:<br /> <br /> Vampires<br /> Werewolves<br /> Mages<br /> Changlings<br /> Spirits<br /> Prometheans<br /> Kitsune<br /> Skinchangers<br /> Demons<br /> Mummies (Maybe... Doubtful though?)<br /> Humans<br /> Gods/Miko for the Gods?<br /> <br /> Not fully Sure though...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T06:49:48-07:00","id":545121,"title":"","content":"There are also the Japanese Lucifuge (or the Rampants) who may be considered as a separate &quot;race&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T08:44:45-07:00","id":545350,"title":"","content":"Not sure how the Bamboo Princess tale reflects on the freehold.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T10:44:54-07:00","id":545524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RickmanUK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/540366-beasts-primordial-s-changeling-spoiler?p=544972#post544972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gods/Miko for the Gods?</div> </div> </div> </div> There's a fair chance that Kami is just another word for Spirit. Though the most powerful may be Emperian.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T11:08:57-07:00","id":545551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/540366-beasts-primordial-s-changeling-spoiler?p=545350#post545350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not sure how the Bamboo Princess tale reflects on the freehold.</div> </div> </div> </div> While I do imagine there might be a Court for each of the Princes/treasures, I do agree I'm not sure of any other particular theme.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T16:41:17-07:00","id":546013,"title":"","content":"Mages, Vamps, Werewolves, Prometheans, Sin-Eaters, Mummies, Demons, Beasts, Ghosts, Sprits, Skinchangers (like Kitsune), Hunters/Lucifuge, I'd say.<br /> <br /> What are the Cursed of Hachiko?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T17:07:51-07:00","id":546112,"title":"","content":"The excerpt, for anyone curious:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beast 99% Draft, p. 384</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Yosei</b><br /> <br /> In Tokyo, many creatures from beyond, youkai, spirits, or perhaps other alien monstrosities, abduct humans. Those few who escape are forever bound to the spiritual realms of their captivity. These survivors, these Yosei, have formed an alliance that spans across the Tokyo Metropolitan Area. The Yosei Court is modeled after the ancient Taketori Monogatari, Tale of the Bamboo Cutter. They follow the leadership of a \u201cMoon Princess\u201d who changes each year, who rules from a seat of Mount Fuji, some 100 kilometers away. She maintains delegates to each of the other creatures of Tokyo; twelve at any given time. Her current delegate to the Children is Akira Hayashi, a former museum archivist who now looks every bit a skeleton with a thin patina of paper flesh. Hayashi mostly appears interested in dealing in artifacts and remnants of Japan\u2019s lost history.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>UnjustCustos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/540366-beasts-primordial-s-changeling-spoiler?p=544857#post544857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">12?! What species are large enough, that didn't get their own book, to require that many?! There are ten including Beast, so if we take out Changeling and hunter we have eight for the main and four that we may not know about. Hmmmmmm.</div> </div> </div> </div>While it implies Beasts have a single delegate, I wouldn't rule out the possibility that some supernaturals may not be deemed high enough priority to get any, and some have more than one. Particularly if at least one type of supernatural has been deemed sufficiently fractious to warrant more than one delegate. Perhaps even just for political reasons. There could be some number of &quot;miscellaneous&quot; delegates, each for several smaller groups of supernaturals.<br /> <br /> Besides, the usual message conveyed by nWoD is that it's a big mysterious place: I could easily believe there are plenty of other supernaturals out there that will never get books of their own.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T17:22:27-07:00","id":546144,"title":"","content":"I forgot hobgoblins, and odds are they would be a group the Lost might consider giving an ambassador.<br /> <br /> The Cursed of Hachiko are a 'minor' template supernatural that is in the Hurt Locker Open Dev stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T17:35:54-07:00","id":546152,"title":"","content":"I could see Forsaken Werewolves and Pure Werewolves having seperate Ambassadors, I don't Ghosts and Spirits would get one, but the Hosts of Toyko might, same with the Luifuge. I hope we get the list of races with an ambassador in Changeling. <br /> <br /> I'll add its also likely on highly organized creatures in Toyko would get a delegrate, Prometheons are too unorganized and to migrant I think.<br /> <br /> I think creatures primarily from another world, Spirits, Hobgoblins, Underworld ghosts don't count as of Toyko to count either.<br /> <br /> Lets see, Demons, Beasts, Vampires, Werewolves/Ferals, Sin Eaters, Mummies, Rampart, Mages, (future races), Immortals, Fae Touched.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T23:31:45-07:00","id":546580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/540366-beasts-primordial-s-changeling-spoiler?p=546144#post546144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I forgot hobgoblins, and odds are they would be a group the Lost might consider giving an ambassador.<br /> <br /> The Cursed of Hachiko are a 'minor' template supernatural that is in the Hurt Locker Open Dev stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div> &quot;Microtemplate&quot; actually- people with themed supernatural merits, <br /> <br /> Close enough to count as kin to a beast I'm sure, but not really a template.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T12:55:05-07:00","id":549199,"title":"","content":"Diamond Orders, Council of Free Assemblies, and Seers could account for three, just for Mages. And even if you consolidate to the Consilium and the Seers, it's two.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T13:03:35-07:00","id":549217,"title":"","content":"Clearly they're leaving the opening for future gamelines - given that it's been mentioned a post-Beast one for next year has already been approved.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T00:16:10-07:00","id":549850,"title":"","content":"Makes sense, they might also be sending delegates to splats that don't warrant their own gamelines- Like kitsune and skinchangers, slashers, the possessed, thaumaturges, shapeshifters, changing breeds, revenants, dark heroes, jackals, alternate vampire types, immortals of various types, etc.<br /> <br /> It's just a matter of deciding or guessing what has enough presence locally to warrant formal recognition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T09:07:46-07:00","id":550237,"title":"","content":"As an Asian, I am really having a lot of problem at Tokyo setting.<br /> I mean, it's like they are going back into that Kindred of the East territory.<br /> The Devs should really either watch less anime, or pander less to anime-fans.<br /> <br /> And this is coming from an anime fan, for god's sake","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1229-torete","name":"torete","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1229_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"125"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T10:33:07-07:00","id":550326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>torete</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/540366-beasts-primordial-s-changeling-spoiler?p=550237#post550237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As an Asian, I am really having a lot of problem at Tokyo setting.<br /> I mean, it's like they are going back into that Kindred of the East territory.<br /> The Devs should really either watch less anime, or pander less to anime-fans.<br /> <br /> And this is coming from an anime fan, for god's sake</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This is of interest to me, as at minimum one of the people writing Tokyo is living in Japan, if not in Tokyo itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T10:39:34-07:00","id":550331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enokh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/540366-beasts-primordial-s-changeling-spoiler?p=550326#post550326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> This is of interest to me, as at minimum one of the people writing Tokyo is living in Japan, if not in Tokyo itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is he/she a native Japanese? I mean, there IS difference it makes there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1229-torete","name":"torete","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1229_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"125"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T10:43:07-07:00","id":550337,"title":"","content":"I've no idea. I'm not even saying you're wrong (I'm not familiar with the setting myself), it's just interesting to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T10:58:35-07:00","id":550347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>torete</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/540366-beasts-primordial-s-changeling-spoiler?p=550237#post550237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As an Asian, I am really having a lot of problem at Tokyo setting.<br /> I mean, it's like they are going back into that Kindred of the East territory.<br /> The Devs should really either watch less anime, or pander less to anime-fans.<br /> <br /> And this is coming from an anime fan, for god's sake</div> </div> </div> </div>What do you feel is pandering? That they have Tokyo as a major setting for every splat? Or that they're including actual Japanese mythological creatures into the Japanese setting?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T11:25:25-07:00","id":550375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>torete</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/540366-beasts-primordial-s-changeling-spoiler?p=550237#post550237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As an Asian, I am really having a lot of problem at Tokyo setting.<br /> I mean, it's like they are going back into that Kindred of the East territory.<br /> The Devs should really either watch less anime, or pander less to anime-fans.<br /> <br /> And this is coming from an anime fan, for god's sake</div> </div> </div> </div>For what it's worth, I watch like... zero anime. Well, not zero. I'm a pretty big Gundam fan. But, that's more or less unrelated. In my experience, I'm not the target market for most anime, and I'm okay with that. There's some I've seen that's kind of neat. There's one called Ghost Hunt that I think is a pretty good model for a World of Darkness chronicle. I do watch a bit of comedy/drama stuff aimed at geeks, like Yusha Yoshihiko and Aoi Hono, but that's not really a big influence on my World of Darkness work. <br /> <br /> My daughters are into Yokai Watch and Sailor Moon. But they're also in elementary school, so I'm not too invested in pandering to them. I watch them sometimes to know what my kids are into. I snuck a really oblique Yokai Watch reference into Changeling, but it's more a joke than anything, and I doubt anyone will catch it. <br /> <br /> For whatever it's worth, I'm curious what you find pandering. I do have a group of Japanese beta readers that read my first drafts, including a colleague that's a folklore specialist. I am not in fact ethnically Japanese, nor do I identify as Japanese; I'm not particularly comfortable 'proving cred', but I've chosen to live here primarily because I spent a good deal of my youth growing up in a Japanese household (I was essentially adopted by my Japanese teacher, which is totally a story out of a shitty 1990s movie, except I mostly learned to play hockey, not karate), and I feel that it's a good experience for my three children.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T11:32:05-07:00","id":550428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/540366-beasts-primordial-s-changeling-spoiler?p=550347#post550347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That they have Tokyo as a major setting for every splat?</div> </div> </div> </div>And for whatever it's worth, this is literally just for three big reasons: <br /> <br /> 1) I like big cosmopolitan setting books. I really loved Chicago. However, those books are wildly impractical, and are unlikely to ever get approved under our current model. So like the way Radar from MASH smuggled a jeep by dismantling it and sending it piece by piece, I'm taking the opportunity to build a setting like that piece by piece. <br /> <br /> 2) I know Tokyo better than any city aside from LA. I feel like LA's gotten plenty of attention from White Wolf over the years, so I wanted to do something different. I really disliked World of Darkness: Tokyo. <br /> <br /> 3) I like to play with conceptual continuity. I like the idea of a little concept that's in a lot of different books. In the case of Tokyo, it's my way of playing with the assumptions of the game lines a little bit. I've been playing and writing these games for a long time. The Tokyo sections of these books are a chance for me to do something different, and both entertain and challenge myself as a writer a little by doing something left of center. <br /> <br /> (Well, also Tokyo's massive population makes it a really viable choice for such a project. But, yeah.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T11:36:55-07:00","id":550430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/540366-beasts-primordial-s-changeling-spoiler?p=549217#post549217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Clearly they're leaving the opening for future gamelines - given that it's been mentioned a post-Beast one for next year has already been approved.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, want to note: Not necessarily true. Like I mentioned in that thread: We do a big project every year for NWoD. It's not always a game line. Dark Eras was last year's. This year's is Beast. Next year's isn't necessarily a game line or whatever. It's just not Fury.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T11:42:46-07:00","id":550432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/540366-beasts-primordial-s-changeling-spoiler?p=550428#post550428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And for whatever it's worth, this is literally just for three big reasons:<br /> <br /> 1) I like big cosmopolitan setting books. I really loved Chicago. However, those books are wildly impractical, and are unlikely to ever get approved under our current model. So like the way Radar from MASH smuggled a jeep by dismantling it and sending it piece by piece, I'm taking the opportunity to build a setting like that piece by piece.<br /> <br /> 2) I know Tokyo better than any city aside from LA. I feel like LA's gotten plenty of attention from White Wolf over the years, so I wanted to do something different. I really disliked World of Darkness: Tokyo.<br /> <br /> 3) I like to play with conceptual continuity. I like the idea of a little concept that's in a lot of different books. In the case of Tokyo, it's my way of playing with the assumptions of the game lines a little bit. I've been playing and writing these games for a long time. The Tokyo sections of these books are a chance for me to do something different, and both entertain and challenge myself as a writer a little by doing something left of center.<br /> <br /> (Well, also Tokyo's massive population makes it a really viable choice for such a project. But, yeah.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I wasn't complaining! I really like that minor thread of continuity you have going and Tokyo is a great city for it. I grew up in LA, live near LA, and lived in Yokosuka for four years, and, while I love LA, Tokyo has the major advantage that you don't need to *drive* but can still get pretty much anywhere (though LA's downtown transportation is getting better).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T12:06:46-07:00","id":550498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/540366-beasts-primordial-s-changeling-spoiler?p=550432#post550432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh, I wasn't complaining! I really like that minor thread of continuity you have going and Tokyo is a great city for it. I grew up in LA, live near LA, and lived in Yokosuka for four years, and, while I love LA, Tokyo has the major advantage that you don't need to *drive* but can still get pretty much anywhere (though LA's downtown transportation is getting better).</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course. I just never really explained that, I figured I'd put it out there. <br /> <br /> And seriously? I was in LA last year for a couple of days. I got stuck in a traffic jam at 4am. It was fucking absurd. But I really miss Oki Dog sometimes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T12:14:02-07:00","id":550504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/540366-beasts-primordial-s-changeling-spoiler?p=550498#post550498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Of course. I just never really explained that, I figured I'd put it out there.<br /> <br /> And seriously? I was in LA last year for a couple of days. I got stuck in a traffic jam at 4am. It was fucking absurd. But I really miss Oki Dog sometimes.</div> </div> </div> </div>They've really expanded things like the light rail system, but it's pretty limited still and traffic is still godawful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T14:30:08-07:00","id":550713,"title":"","content":"Even more super excited if we get some Changeling info in the new book on Tokyo.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/448-dulahan","name":"Dulahan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar448_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"115"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T16:09:46-07:00","id":550848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dulahan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/540366-beasts-primordial-s-changeling-spoiler?p=550713#post550713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even more super excited if we get some Changeling info in the new book on Tokyo.</div> </div> </div> </div>Truth be told, it's like... the only thing I haven't finished in first drafts. Mostly because it's my section, and I manage it differently than the stuff I edit for the rest of the team. But, I may post it once it's ready.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T16:14:17-07:00","id":550850,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/540366-beasts-primordial-s-changeling-spoiler?p=550504#post550504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They've really expanded things like the light rail system, but it's pretty limited still and traffic is still godawful.</div> </div> </div> </div>Limited yes, but as someone without a car it's a-hell-of-a-lot better than it used to be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T17:59:39-07:00","id":550929,"title":"","content":"The closest I've been to Japan is the Rachel &amp; Jun and the Texan in Tokyo channels on Youtube, so I can't talk too much about how it compares to the actual place. But, I have two points I <i>can</i> comment on.<br /> <br /> 1) I am an anime fan, and I have never once felt like the Tokyo setting has pandered to me. Nothing really feels like an anime. Like, we have kaiju there? But those are magath, and aren't as big an element as the struggle with the Uratha's (spiritual) Ainu identity. I don't want to claim I can smell an anime setup anywhere, buuuuut I can say I don't really smell it in the WoD sections.<br /> <br /> 2) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/324537-2nd-edition-weekly-discussion-the-onmyodo-mage-in-tokyo?p=326764#post326764\">After Dave's discussion with Wyrdhamster on the Mage forums about how the samurai icon isn't really a thing with the modern Japanese populace</a>(Start at link and continue onward), I don't have much reason to doubt Dave and his goals in portraying the city and the people. I'm not in the position to say if he's succeeding or not, but it at least has versimilitude for myself as a skeptic of most portrayals of Japan from an American creator. Because of the anime.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 06-11-2015, 09:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T19:06:57-07:00","id":550981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/540366-beasts-primordial-s-changeling-spoiler?p=550929#post550929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The closest I've been to Japan is the Rachel &amp; Jun and the Texan in Tokyo channels on Youtube, so I can't talk too much about how it compares to the actual place. But, I have two points I <i>can</i> comment on.<br /> <br /> 1) I am an anime fan, and I have never once felt like the Tokyo setting has pandered to me. Nothing really feels like an anime. Like, we have kaiju there? But those are magath, and aren't as big an element as the struggle with the Uratha's (spiritual) Ainu identity. I don't want to claim I can smell an anime setup anywhere, buuuuut I can say I don't really smell it in the WoD sections.<br /> <br /> 2) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/324537-2nd-edition-weekly-discussion-the-onmyodo-mage-in-tokyo?p=326764#post326764\">After Dave's discussion with Wyrdhamster on the Mage forums about how the samurai icon isn't really a thing with the modern Japanese populace</a>(Start at link and continue onward), I don't have much reason to doubt Dave and his goals in portraying the city and the people. I'm not in the position to say if he's succeeding or not, but it at least has versimilitude for myself as a skeptic of most portrayals of Japan from an American creator. Because of the anime.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fetishisation of Japanese culture is a thing I face all the time. It's a pretty significant portion of the younger Western population in Japan. They have a few recurring behaviors that are just plain abhorrent; and dealing with the Japanese on a colleague or friendly basis, you have to hear their opinions on <i>that guy</i>. I love Japan. It'd take some remarkable offer to make me leave. But like, &quot;the ancient arts of samurai geisha naruto katana ninjutsu&quot; are just not a part of my experience here at all. <br /> <br /> And side note: If you like Rachel &amp; Jun, I recommend you watch Gimmeaflakeman. He's an older guy, I believe he's ethnically Peruvian but from America. He sheds very adult, very 'not invested in otaku culture' perspectives about Japan. I also like Unrested; he's also professionally active in the tabletop game industry. He does a great job of retelling folklore and urban legends. I particularly like him because he focuses a lot on more modern stories. His Youtube channel is great fodder for World of Darkness stories in general, but with a Japanese flair. They're also super cool people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T21:03:07-07:00","id":551049,"title":"","content":"I just want to toss out there that I love the notion of Changeling Freeholds being centred around a foundational story, and that narrative weaves its way even into <i>that</i> aspect of their being. It helps establish the kinds of narrative(s) that might revolve around that place, gives an idea of its morals, its values, the things it respects and disdains, etc.<br /> <br /> A Freehold in Northern Ireland based around the Giant's Causeway may tell a variant of such a tale, and hold in value guile over strength; mental agility and guile may be held in vogue over martial displays, with the Summer Court (or any martial equivalent court) primarily made up of gifted Renard-esque tricksters and tacticians than the brutes others elsewhere may be used to.<br /> <br /> As an aside, this is making me want to hammer some more on my homebrew version of Miami. Very much shuns the &quot;Focus on the actual&quot; kind of work that OP is putting into its settings lately (don't get me wrong, I love that) and instead turns the whole thing into Miami Vice fan fiction, you might say, but that's a part of Changeling; getting lost in a narrative.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T21:45:08-07:00","id":551078,"title":"","content":"In about two weeks, I'll finally begin building Paris's courts. I can't wait.<br /> <br /> That only has so much relevance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T14:33:27-07:00","id":552183,"title":"","content":"after reading the Court System preview, I wonder if sending the Huntsmen after impossible quests is the Freehold's Approach, or that the changelings themselves being sent to search after hidden treasures is the Freehold's Bulwark. I assume that either way, the treasures are tied to the 12 supernatural races they have ambassadors to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T17:50:17-07:00","id":552383,"title":"","content":"Probably.<br /> <br /> The &quot;treasures&quot; could include tokens, enchanted items, fetishes, and the like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Currently Playing:</b> <i>A large, mixed splat game of <b>CofD</b>.</i> <b>As:</b> Seraph du Salomon, Voice on the concordance. Unsubtle man reluctantly participating in the business of Magi. Awakening 2E homebrew <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1338514-house-du-salomon-a-proximus-dynasty?_=1569864567692\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...=1569864567692</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2598-gryphon-s-feather","name":"Gryphon's Feather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2598_3.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"215"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T17:54:09-07:00","id":552386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/540366-beasts-primordial-s-changeling-spoiler?p=552183#post552183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">after reading the Court System preview, I wonder if sending the Huntsmen after impossible quests is the Freehold's Approach,</div> </div> </div> </div>From what we've seen, I'm not sure there <i>is</i> a Freehold-wide Approach:* each Approach seems to be particular to its Court's ideal and emotion. I could see something like impossible quests for Huntsmen in an Approach, but they seem to be focused more on individuals. Each Approach we've seen is focused on a Huntsman attacking, entrapping, isolating, or unbalancing a particular Changeling or group of Changelings, rather than the Court as a whole, using methods that undermine the Court's associated emotion and/or strengths. I feel like it would need some kind of context to narrow it down to some way that the Huntsman is thwarting one/some Changelings on an individual level<br /> <br /> If there's a Court that prides itself on its ability to pursue storied wonders, maybe a Huntsman's Approach might involve beating such a questing Changeling to the prize. The Huntsman might get Yearning then and there, or may need to then destroy it, use it to claim whatever benefit the Changeling would have been due, or manipulate the unsuccessful Changeling with it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> or that the changelings themselves being sent to search after hidden treasures is the Freehold's Bulwark. I assume that either way, the treasures are tied to the 12 supernatural races they have ambassadors to. </div> </div> </div>The Bulwark I could definitely see. I'm not sure who or what might &quot;officiate,&quot; but the idea of pursuing rare treasures is cool and fitting; perhaps the greatest of these brought in a given year's hunt becomes the &quot;Moon Princess&quot; for the year, but heaven help them if not a one brings any treasure worthy of qualifying.<br /> <br /> The 12 ambassadors could have some connection, but I'm not so sure about that. I can't find any reference to 12 in the Tale of the Bamboo Cutter, which makes me think there's another reason for the number. This could be that there's some oath or other magical reason for keeping 12 ambassadors. Or this could simply be a case where there's no mystic significance to the number, and this simply meets the diplomatic needs of the Freehold with Tokyo's supernatural communities. To be honest, I've got a hunch it's the latter.<br /> <br /> * I could be wrong!<br /> <br /> For reference, a compiled listing of all example Approaches:<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>Brass:</b><br /> <u>It's a Trap!:</u> Brass courtiers know how dangerous the hedge is and delve in anyways. Huntsmen gain a point of Yearning when they arrange for courtiers to fall into a trap in the hedge. This may be an ambush, planting a red-herring to derail their quest, or altering a trod to lead them into dangerous territory.<br /> <u>Foundation of Sand:</u> Not everyone's faith is built upon a firm foundation. Huntsmen gain a point of Yearning when they attack and manage to shake a courtier's faith. It might engage a character in a debate, or use her faith to manipulate her by creating false signs and evidence only to reveal the deception at a critical point.<br /> <br /> <b>Ivory:</b><br /> <u>Betrayal from Within:</u> When recruiting mortals, someone untrustworthy will inevitably slip past any safeguards that are in place. Huntsmen gain a point of Yearning when they manipulate a mortal pledged to an Ivory Courtier into breaking their oath.<br /> <u>All that Glisters is Not Gold:</u> Greed is many courtiers' undoing, even if they claim mastery over it. Huntsmen gain a point of Yearning when they entrap an Ivory courtier through their greed.<br /> <br /> <b>Jade:</b><br /> <u>Mortal Influence:</u> When a Jade courtier finds herself in a position of influence in mortal affairs, Huntsmen gain a point of Yearning to turn these relationships against the changelings. A lawyer may find herself accused of misconduct and disbarred while a florist might find her greenhouse SWATed by police looking for drugs.<br /> <u>The Fall:</u> Nothing builds pride and confidence like a well laid plan. Huntsmen gain a point of Yearning when disrupting a plan made by a Jade courtier.<br /> <br /> <b>Silver:</b><br /> <u>Checkmate:</u> The Wild Hunt is attempting to play the Huntsmen's own game. Hunstmen gain a point of Yearning when they allow a Silver courtier to learn one of their plots only to turn it around against the changeling.<br /> <u>Temper Tantrum:</u> In embracing wrath, some courtiers fail to also cultivate patience and the clear sight to apply it appropriately. Huntsmen gain a point of Yearning when they drive a Silver courtier into a blind rage.<br /> <br /> <b>Copper:</b><br /> <u>Union Buster:</u> One hundred years ago, vibrant workers unions dominated the mining industry. Though the mines and unions are gone, the Huntsmen still have an open Approach in the form of attacking the courtier\u2019s alliances. A Huntsman gains a point of Yearning when it manipulates the character\u2019s employer to make the changeling\u2019s life miserable, or befriends their mortal friends and use gossip to turn those relationships against the changeling.<br /> <u>The Craftsman\u2019s Hammer:</u> Craftsmen in the Copper Court are proud of their work and well respected for their skill, but it also creates an Approach. A Huntsman gains a point of Yearning when turning a changeling\u2019s creation against them. This can be done by wielding one of the character\u2019s axes in battle, framing her by stealing her customized pistol and leaving it at a scene of a crime or even sabotaging a carpenter\u2019s work so his clients will sue him.<br /> <u>Might Have Been:</u> Regret may be the emotion the court has claimed, but if a changeling isn\u2019t careful it can swallow her whole and destroy her. A Huntsman gains a point of Yearning when they dangle the possibility of regaining something that was lost in front of their target. A courtier who regrets not being there to see their child growing up might be offered the chance to have the Huntsman\u2019s help ousting their fetch and smoothing the way back into their lives in exchange for betraying someone else.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T13:33:18-07:00","id":553367,"title":"","content":"Hm...<br /> <br /> What kind of Bulwark, do you think, would a single-Court freehold have (as in, the Winter Court)?<br /> <br /> I'm making a version of Bishopgate from <i>Asylum </i>that's become home to a gaggle of Winter changelings under the wary, paranoid eyes of a fearful Queen-the head nurse.<br /> <br /> Something to do with madness or ghosts, perhaps?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T19:21:35-07:00","id":553644,"title":"","content":"Obviously, one of the races is going to be talking cats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T20:12:21-07:00","id":553682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/540366-beasts-primordial-s-changeling-spoiler?p=553644#post553644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Obviously, one of the races is going to be talking cats.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>what are you doing reading my secret list of embarrassing rpg desires and how are you breaking into my room</i>[/sarcasm]","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T06:34:02-07:00","id":555577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RickmanUK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/540366-beasts-primordial-s-changeling-spoiler?p=544972#post544972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I believe in Japan Humans Would count as a seperate Species, I think it would be something like:<br /> <br /> Vampires<br /> Werewolves<br /> Mages<br /> Changlings<br /> Spirits<br /> Prometheans<br /> Kitsune<br /> Skinchangers<br /> Demons<br /> Mummies (Maybe... Doubtful though?)<br /> Humans<br /> Gods/Miko for the Gods?<br /> <br /> Not fully Sure though...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Traditionally, Japanese don't bury their dead, or at least they didn't use to do so. Not sure how many Mummies you'd find over there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T06:42:22-07:00","id":555582,"title":"","content":"Japanese funeral practices would have no bearing on mummies whatsoever, because they're all from a civilization that existed somewhere in northeast Africa.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T18:47:12-07:00","id":557690,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/540366-beasts-primordial-s-changeling-spoiler?p=555577#post555577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Traditionally, Japanese don't bury their dead, or at least they didn't use to do so. Not sure how many Mummies you'd find over there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep. That's why when the undead apocalypse comes, I'll be safe. Sorry, y'all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T19:44:09-07:00","id":557749,"title":"","content":"Hopefully I can get there then","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCxrkv14ojD_TQXU0RBvF33Q\" target=\"_blank\">Fool's Corner Productions</a>: Where we review Video Game, and eventually tabletop RPGs<br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img31/2512/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/461-kingcarnival","name":"KingCarnival","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar461_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T14:30:19-07:00","id":561212,"title":"","content":"Depends on the type. If its a Brian Keene types your still doomed.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Spoilers<br /> <br /> <br /> One type is dead bodies possessed by sentient beings created before the current universe so they can sail to Japan, and the others I think infects birds earily on so bird zombies will be coming for you.<br /> <br /> Sadly most of what I know about Japan comes from Japanese Porn. I can discuss, Pink Salons, and genres of Japanese porn, but outside that sort of thing I'm lost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T16:47:48-07:00","id":561343,"title":"","content":"There are probably Mummies (as in Mummy: the Curse) in Japan; there definitely are in China. Mummies cultivate cults of mortal followers to deal with things like what happens to their body in the event that they get put down. Plus, in a worst-case scenario, they can actually totally survive even if their body is completely incinerated, reforming from a preserved organ elsewhere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T12:28:28-07:00","id":565610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/540366-beasts-primordial-s-changeling-spoiler?p=550428#post550428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) I know Tokyo better than any city aside from LA. I feel like LA's gotten plenty of attention from White Wolf over the years, so I wanted to do something different. I really disliked World of Darkness: Tokyo.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know little about the city beside bits and pieces from films, anime and the occasional blog read or wiki search (not even much of the last two back then) and still hated that books with the burning wrath of a 1000 suns. Hong Kong was a far from great product of its times (far too much &quot;run to the hills the chins/commies are coming!&quot; leaking through the pages) but the Tokyo book was awful. It was a disservice to the city, to WtO and KotE, honestly. Whoever wrote it didn't even care to make the NPCs make sense to what they were <b>supposed</b> to be....<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T19:19:56-07:00","id":565970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/540366-beasts-primordial-s-changeling-spoiler?p=555577#post555577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Traditionally, Japanese don't bury their dead, or at least they didn't use to do so. Not sure how many Mummies you'd find over there.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sokushinbutsu\" target=\"_blank\">It's not the burial practices you need to be worried about.</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/210-siven","name":"Siven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}